  "overuseNoticeTitle": "Medication days at a reference level",
  "@overuseNoticeTitle": {
    "description": "[medical] Title of the notice shown when acute-medication days reached the ICHD-3 medication-overuse reference level in each of the last 3 months. Calm and factual; not a warning or a diagnosis."
  },
  "overuseNoticeBody": "In each of the last 3 complete months, your days with acute medication reached a level that headache guidelines (ICHD-3) use when looking at medication-overuse headache, where frequent use of acute medication can make headaches more frequent. This is a count of what you logged, not a diagnosis. Don't change how you take a medication because of it; it may be worth discussing with your doctor.",
  "@overuseNoticeBody": {
    "description": "[medical] Body of the medication-overuse notice. It must not say the user has medication-overuse headache, and must not tell them to stop or change a medication. Needs a second reviewer."
  },
